# Cursor Cloud specific instructions

`AGENTS.md` is at its line cap, so Cloud Agent instructions live here.

## Setup

If `uv` is missing or `.venv` is absent, run `bash .cursor/install.sh`. It is
idempotent. The CLI and git-hook tests need no database or Docker. Don't start
Docker Compose.

## Verify

Before editing, name the test that should fail and run it to show the failure.
After editing, run the focused tests, then the area suite:

```bash
uv run pytest -q scripts/tests/test_attribution.py
uv run pytest -q cli/tests/test_agent_guide.py cli/tests/test_cli_help.py
uv run ruff check . && uv run ruff format --check .
uv run python scripts/add_spdx.py --check
uv run python scripts/check_docs.py --base origin/demo/cursor-agentic-sdlc
```

`scripts/tests/test_attribution.py` takes 2 to 7 minutes on a Cloud Agent VM.
While developing, run one test with `-k <name>`; run the whole file once before
you push. Paste the pass and fail counts into the pull request.

## Pull requests

- Base every pull request on `demo/cursor-agentic-sdlc`, never `main`.
- Open it as a draft. A person marks it ready, which starts CI.
- Title it as a Conventional Commit, such as `fix(cli): ...`.
- Fill in the repository's pull request template. Leave unverified items
  unchecked.
- A repository hook denies force pushes, hard resets, and pushes to `main`.
  Push new commits instead.
